quack: RL training environments for Microduck, a ~800 g, 25 cm bipedal robot with 14 Dynamixel XL330 servos. Built on mjlab (MuJoCo Warp) + PPO (rsl_rl). Policies train at 50 Hz and export to ONNX for the robot runtime (robotd/robotctl, a separate repo). Servos are simulated with the BAM XL330 voltage/friction model; at this scale actuator fidelity is most of the sim2real gap.

SETUP

Needs a CUDA GPU, uv, make.

    git clone https://github.com/sueszli/quack && cd quack
    make sync
    make tests

WORKFLOW

    make envs                                                  # list tasks
    make smoke                                                 # 64 envs, 5 iters; run before every long run
    make train                                                 # 4096 envs, 6000 iters, ~1-2 h for a usable gait
    make play CKPT=logs/rsl_rl/velocity/<run>/model_3000.pt    # headless GPU: ARGS="--viewer viser" serves a browser viewer on :8080
    make export CKPT=3000                                      # -> weights/output.onnx, obs normalizer baked in
    make infer                                                 # CPU MuJoCo deployment rehearsal
    make train ARGS="--agent.resume True --agent.load-checkpoint model_3000.pt"

The make targets hardcode Mjlab-Velocity-Flat-MicroDuck. For other tasks call the tools directly:

    uv run train <TASK> --env.scene.num-envs 64 --agent.max_iterations 5
    uv run train <TASK> --env.scene.num-envs 4096 --agent.max_iterations 6000
    uv run play <TASK> --checkpoint-file logs/rsl_rl/<exp>/<run>/model_N.pt
    uv run export <TASK> --checkpoint N

Checkpoints land in logs/rsl_rl/<exp>/<run>/ (<exp> is the cfg's experiment_name). `--checkpoint N` picks the newest run; `--checkpoint-file <path>` for any run. Always deploy ONNX from `uv run export`, never a hand-converted checkpoint.

TASKS

  Mjlab-Velocity-{Flat,Rough}-MicroDuck    walking, velocity + head-pose commands (main task)
  Mjlab-VelStand-{Flat,Rough}-MicroDuck    walking + fall recovery
  Mjlab-StandUp-{Flat,Rough}-MicroDuck     stand up from the ground, then body-pose control
  Mjlab-SitStand-{Flat,Rough}-MicroDuck    commanded sit <-> stand
  Mjlab-GroundPick-{Flat,Rough}-MicroDuck  crouch, touch the ground with the mouth, stand back up
  Mjlab-BallKick-Flat-MicroDuck            kick a ball forward
  Mjlab-Roulade-Flat-MicroDuck             forward roll, land on feet
  Mjlab-Velocity-Flat-MicroDuck-Rollers    roller-skate velocity tracking
  Mjlab-Velocity-Swizzle-MicroDuck         swizzle skating
  Mjlab-RollerCrouch-Flat-MicroDuck        crouch while gliding on rollers
  Mjlab-RollerSlope-Flat-MicroDuck         glide down slopes on rollers
  Mjlab-RollerStandUp-Flat-MicroDuck       stand up onto the wheels
  Mjlab-Spin-Flat-MicroDuck                spin in place on rollers

Backlash variants: insert `-Backlash` before `MicroDuck` (e.g. Mjlab-Velocity-Flat-Backlash-MicroDuck) to train on a model with +-1 deg of gear play per servo. Same obs/action dims. Not for Roulade, RollerStandUp, Spin. See src/task_backlash.py.

DEPLOYMENT REHEARSAL

The runtime hot-swaps policies behind a shared 61-D observation contract. Rehearse that on CPU:

    uv run infer --walking walk.onnx --standing stand.onnx --sitstand sitstand.onnx --roulade roulade.onnx --new-cmd-obs

Keyboard: velocity commands, G ground pick, Y sit/stand, R roulade, K/L kicks. `--new-cmd-obs` is required for current policies; forgetting it fails silently. `--debug`, `--save-csv`, `--record` for sim2real comparisons. `--no-bam` swaps the BAM actuators for the XML PD ones.

PUBLISHING

`uv run publish` uploads policy.onnx + manifest.json + README to the Hugging Face Hub in the shape the robot daemon loads. Needs `hf auth login` unless `--dry-run`.

    uv run publish --task Mjlab-BallKick-Flat-MicroDuck --checkpoint 3000 --repo <user>/microduck-kick --kind episodic --duration-s 4.0
    uv run publish --onnx out.onnx --repo <user>/microduck-flamingo --kind perpetual --unwind-s 1.5
    uv run publish --onnx out.onnx --repo <user>/microduck-my-walk --kind perpetual --slot walk
    uv run publish --onnx out.onnx --repo <user>/microduck-kick --kind episodic --duration-s 4.0 --dry-run

`--kind episodic` runs for `--duration-s` and returns to standing. `--kind perpetual` runs until stopped: a gait (`--slot walk|stand`) or a held pose (`--unwind-s`). Not publishable: GroundPick (phase-driven) and SitStand (posture flag), the daemon owns those.

On the robot:

    sudo robotctl policy add kick <user>/microduck-kick
    sudo robotctl policy add flamingo <user>/microduck-flamingo --hold 5
    sudo robotctl policy load walk <user>/microduck-my-walk
    robotctl robot do kick

CONVENTIONS

- 61-D actor obs shared by every policy: 48 proprioception + commands [twist(3), head_pose(4), body_pose(6)]. Unused command slots are zero-padded, never removed.
- Joints: 0-4 left leg, 5-8 neck/head, 9-13 right leg. Unactuated joints are named passive_*; servo selectors use `^(?!passive_).*`.
- ENABLE_* toggles (e.g. ENABLE_SYMMETRY) at the top of cfg files.
